OL,3,AMcCartney and Starr back new Beatles
OL,4,Aattraction
OL,5,
OL,6,FSir Paul McCartney and Ringo Starr have
OL,7,Fbacked plans for a major new Beatles
OL,8,Fvisitor attraction in Liverpool.
OL,10,FThe development will see The Beatles
OL,11,FStory move from Albert Dock to the
OL,12,Fformer St John's Market site, alongside
OL,13,Fa new Yellow Submarine experience at St
OL,14,FJohn's Beacon.
OL,16,FMcCartney said he "can't wait" for
OL,17,Fpeople to be able to "step into our
OL,18,Fstory", while Starr said: "Liverpool
OL,19,Fwas, and still is, Music City".
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
